    "description": "What Sri Lanka calls non-alignment is, in practice, something closer to strategic ambiguity, a refusal to make choices dressed up as a principled refusal to take sides. In a post-Trump world, where great powers weaponise trade, technology and supply chains as instruments of coercion, the President\u2019s posture leaves us exposed.",
