    "md5": "232aa2de6dadfc8de6180f95c05ca4d6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1874,
    "chunk_text": "The truth about personal branding\n\nIn today\u2019s competitive business world, having a good product is not enough. There are so many products and services available in the market, all trying to attract more customers. As a consequence, customers are becoming more discerning, not just with what they want to buy but also with whom they want to buy it from. In this, we find another great truth applicable to modern entrepreneurship: before buying a product, people tend to \"buy\" the person behind that product.\n\nPersonal branding is one area that comes into play here. Personal branding is basically how a person presents themselves to the world. It consists of their values, their personality, their communication style, and their ability to create a certain impression on people. Personal branding is not just about promoting one\u2019s self as an entrepreneur but rather about building trust with customers.\n\nAn important reason why personal branding is important is the value of trust in the purchasing process. In today\u2019s environment, people are often surrounded by ads, which makes them skeptical about marketing. Therefore, they do not rely on marketing; instead, they want the story of the business, the entrepreneur, and the business itself. When the entrepreneur is open, people develop trust, which helps them feel connected with the business.\n\nAn important aspect of this is the psychological aspect of the people involved. People do not develop connections with products; they develop connections with people. A person has feelings, has gone through experiences, and has a story, while a product is just a simple object. The entrepreneur develops an emotional connection with the people by sharing their story, their struggles, their inspirations, and their achievements. Price, features, etc., may not influence the purchasing decision as much as this connection."
  },
