    "md5": "9b3be70e24ec89b9a41c570a18a27423",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1828,
    "chunk_text": "An important aspect of this is the psychological aspect of the people involved. People do not develop connections with products; they develop connections with people. A person has feelings, has gone through experiences, and has a story, while a product is just a simple object. The entrepreneur develops an emotional connection with the people by sharing their story, their struggles, their inspirations, and their achievements. Price, features, etc., may not influence the purchasing decision as much as this connection.\n\nFor example, today, it has become quite common for businesses, especially small ones, to grow through social media sites such as Instagram or TikTok, not only because of the product but also because of the person behind the product. It is natural that the customers would want to know the process of how the product is being made, and the business would feel more relatable as they are able to show the hard work that goes behind the product.\n\nOne advantage that can be derived from differentiation is personal branding. The product can easily be replicated in the market. The competitors may even offer similar features, designs, or even a low-cost advantage. The personal brand, on the other hand, is difficult to replicate. Every entrepreneur has a unique voice, viewpoint, and story to tell. He/she is able to create a unique identity that differentiates him/her from competitors in the market through personal branding.\n\nYoung business owners or those with little funding will benefit a great deal from this. Creating a personal brand does not require one to spend a fortune. It requires consistency, sincerity, and communication. The business owners will not need to spend a fortune on advertising as they create a strong personal brand that attracts more customers through insightful communication."
  },
