    "chunk_text": "In recognition of his contributions to business and technology, Muthukumarana was named among Echelon Magazine\u2019s Top 100 Next-Generation Business Leaders of Sri Lanka (NE100) in 2019. He has played an active role in shaping Sri Lanka\u2019s digital economy through SLASSCOM, serving on national advisory committees for Intelligent Automation, and ICT Capacity Building, and as a General Council Member.\n\nDr. Pieries is a senior corporate leader with over two decades of professional experience across multiple sectors including energy, lubricants, logistics, telecommunications, banking, insurance, and customer service. He has extensive experience in business transformation, strategic leadership, brand development, and operational management, having held several senior leadership roles within the LAUGFS Group.\n\nPrior to assuming his current role, Dr. Pieries served as the Director/Chief Executive Officer of LAUGFS Lubricants Ltd., and LAUGFS Car Care and Petroleum, where he led the organisation through a successful business transformation and expansion phase. Under his leadership, the brand strengthened its market presence and expanded into regional markets including Bangladesh and the Maldives, while achieving significant improvements in operational and financial performance.\n\nDr. Pieries holds doctoral qualifications in business and management, together with a Master of Business Administration from Edith Cowan University, Australia. He is also a Fellow Member of the Institute of Certified Management Accountants of Sri Lanka (CMA), and a Certified Management Accountant.\n\nIn addition to his corporate responsibilities, Dr. Pieries contributes to academia as a senior lecturer in management and leadership, supporting the development of future business professionals in a number of local and international institutes and universities."
