    "chunk_size_bytes": 2017,
    "chunk_text": "Prym Intimates expands global footprint with new manufacturing facility in Vietnam\n\nPrym Intimates, a division of the Germany-based William Prym Group, has opened its newest manufacturing facility in Hung Yen, Vietnam, in close proximity to Hanoi.\n\nThe plant commenced operations on 3 March 2026 and marks the company\u2019s fourth manufacturing location globally.\n\nThe William Prym Group, established in 1530, is one of the world\u2019s oldest family-owned industrial companies operating four divisions at present, with Prym Intimates serving the global intimate apparel sector.\n\nPrym Intimates specialises in manufacturing accessories used in intimate apparel, including components for bras and related products and operates manufacturing facilities in Sri Lanka, China and Indonesia.\n\nThe new Vietnam facility strengthens Prym Intimates\u2019 global production network, enabling the company to serve intimate apparel brands and vendors across key sourcing regions. With manufacturing spanning four countries, customers can source accessories closer to their garment production locations, helping reduce lead times and increase supply chain flexibility.\n\nPrym Intimates Divisional Head Vasu Wijegoonawardane said in today\u2019s increasingly volatile and fast-moving market environment, speed and agility have become critical for success. Prym Intimates\u2019 expanded manufacturing footprint allows brands and vendors to respond quickly to changing customer demands while benefiting from reliable and efficient supply.\n\nOperating across multiple locations, Prym Intimates ensures consistent product quality and service standards worldwide through standardised manufacturing platforms, processes and technology across all facilities, allowing customers to source from any Prym location with confidence.\n\nRecognised for its innovation, design capabilities and continuous product development, the company focuses on anticipating market changes, adapting quickly, and delivering solutions that create value for its business partners."
