    "chunk_text": "At the recent Raisina dialogue the US representative openly said that America would not allow India to do as China did and use the present world economic order to rise peacefully to become an economic challenge to the West. India would be na\u00efve to think that being an uncritical buddy of Israel and junior partner of the US, will save it.\n\nInsisted on putting \u2018politics in command\u2019\u2014grasping politics, not economics, as \u2018the key link\u2019.\n\nAlways posed the question \u2018Who Are Our Friends, Who Are Our Enemies?\u2019\n\nLucidly distinguished \u2018antagonistic contradictions\u2019 (those between oneself and one\u2019s enemy) from \u2018non-antagonistic contradictions\u2019 (those among friends), and knew that the former couldn\u2019t be resolved peacefully.\n\nEmphasised the importance of, and support for, wars of National Liberation against imperialism.\n\nThe US gives Israel advanced weapons as \u2018assistance\u2019; it doesn\u2019t sell them. Whatever the faults of the USSR and PRC, they aided Vietnam militarily, enabling the latter to defend its airspace and contest the US Air Force. That has not been so with Iran.\n\nIf a Third World War targeting China is to be avoided down the road, one of three outcomes is needed in Iran:\n\nA hurting stalemate causes a cessation of hostilities and a return to\u00a0 negotiations, but with irreversibly firm guarantees.\n\nThe US is trapped in a quagmire with casualties unacceptable to the voting public.\n\nThe US stops its war and withdraws its offensive formations deployed against Iran.\n\nAll this is far from an abstraction for Sri Lanka. It is a matter of the most pressing and glaringly obvious relevance. As the Newsweek cover story about the USA against China concludes:"
