    "chunk_text": "The timing could not be more relevant. The central leadership challenge of our era is no longer simply managing change; it is leading with human purpose through technological disruption. As AI accelerates the pace of decision-making and reshapes roles across every industry, organisations are discovering that their greatest gap is not digital capability. It is the human capacity to lead with clarity, communicate with authenticity, and hold teams together with a compelling sense of direction. Algorithms cannot do that. Purposeful leaders can.\n\nThe upcoming programme will be held on 15 and 16 May and 12 and 13 June 2026 at the Hilton Colombo Residencies (JAIC), Colombo 2. The participation fee is Rs. 62,000, with an early bird rate of Rs. 52,000 for fully paid registrations before 5 April 2026. Group discounts apply, and NLP Practitioner Certifications are awarded to qualifying participants.\n\nWhether you are a past participant ready to experience a deeper dimension, or a leader encountering Mastery of Self for the first time, this is a rare opportunity to invest in the capability that matters most in a high-tech world: purposeful human leadership. Daily FT, Sri Lanka\u2019s leading business daily and a long-standing supporter of leadership development initiatives that have made a measurable difference to Sri Lankan businesses, is proud to be the Business Media Sponsor of this program.\n\nTo download the brochure or register, visit www.ranjandesilva.com/mastery-of-self or contact +94 76 660 3227."
