    "md5": "a79b478d8ec7d0f9fe562579151e429e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1692,
    "chunk_text": "Home Lands breaks ground on Canterbury Crest Resort Apartments\n\nFinal phase construction commences of the largest residential development project in Sri Lanka\n\nHome Lands has officially begun development of Canterbury Crest Resort Apartments following the ceremonial groundbreaking and foundation stone laying.\n\nThis occasion marks the launch of one of four brand-new resort apartment developments by Home Lands in Greater Colombo. Canterbury Crest is the last stage of development at Canterbury Golf City - Piliyandala Kahaththuduwa, the largest residential development project in Sri Lanka comprising 1,200 units already. Due to the strong market demand generated by Canterbury Golf City, Home Lands made the strategic decision to introduce this final phase of resort apartments complementing Sri Lanka\u2019s largest residential development.\n\nThe ceremony, held on 19 March, was graced by Home Lands Group Chairman Nalin Herath, together with the management.\n\nCanterbury Golf City is Sri Lanka\u2019s first Victorian-style golf resort apartments and residencies complex, a defining milestone in Home Lands\u2019 journey. With the addition of Canterbury Crest, Home Lands continues to meet the rising demand for residential living inside this prestigious development, building on the success of other projects within Canterbury Golf City such as Canterbury Golf Resort Apartments, Canterbury Garden Resort Apartments, Canterbury Lexus, Canterbury Golf Villas and Canterbury Golf Residencies.\u00a0 The project is symbolic of Home Lands\u2019 ability to combine scale, design excellence, and lifestyle innovation, establishing a benchmark that became a blueprint for the company\u2019s subsequent developments."
  },
