    "chunk_size_bytes": 1112,
    "chunk_text": "NSB partners with IIHS to expand healthcare education access\n\nThe National Savings Bank (NSB) has partnered with the International Institute of Health Sciences (IIHS) to improve access to global healthcare education for Sri Lankan students.\n\nUnder a new MoU, NSB will provide student loan facilities through its island-wide branch network, enabling students from diverse backgrounds to enroll in IIHS programmes. These include Nursing, Physiotherapy, Biomedical Sciences, and International Foundation courses leading to globally recognized qualifications.\n\n\u201cWe view education financing as a vital investment in the country\u2019s future,\u201d said NSB Acting General Manager Devika Silva.\n\nThe initiative aims to reduce foreign exchange outflows from overseas education while strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s role as a regional healthcare education hub.\n\nITC Ratnadipa presents Easter Brunch on April 5 at Indian Ocean Pavilion\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
