    "chunk_text": "EWIS launches AI platform to tackle legacy system risk\n\nSri Lankan technology firm EWIS has unveiled EWIS AEGIS, an AI-powered platform designed to de-risk the modernisation of mission-critical legacy systems.\n\nTargeting sectors such as banking, healthcare, and government, the platform addresses the high costs and operational disruptions traditionally associated with updating core infrastructure. EWIS AEGIS employs a simulation-first approach, utilising AI-driven code intelligence and digital twin technology to replicate and validate system behaviour before any changes are implemented.\n\nThis proprietary system, for which a patent is pending, allows organisations to predict outcomes and identify risks in advance. EWIS Chairman Sanjeewa Wickramanayake stated the platform enables businesses to \u201cmove from uncertainty to control.\u201d\n\nEngineered in Sri Lanka for global markets, EWIS AEGIS aims to deliver greater cost predictability and reduced downtime for enterprises undertaking large-scale digital transformation.\n\nCap Snap Lanka secures six international certifications in six months\n\nITC Ratnadipa presents Easter Brunch on April 5 at Indian Ocean Pavilion\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
