    "chunk_text": "KOKO wins Overall Gold at LankaPay Technnovation Awards 2026\n\nKOKO has secured the Overall Gold Award for Excellence in Digital Payments at the LankaPay Technnovation Awards 2026 \u2013 a remarkable feat in its first year of participation.\n\nThe company also bagged three category Gold Awards: Best Enabler for LankaSign Digital Signatures, Most Popular Digital Payment Solution, and Best Digital Payment App for Retail Payments. It was additionally shortlisted for Best Institution for Financial Inclusivity.\n\nDuring the year under review, KOKO enabled approximately LKR 4 billion in transactions, recorded 100,000 registered JustPay users, and supported 1,200 merchants \u2013 achieving an 846% year-on-year growth in users and merchants.\n\nLankaPay CEO Channa de Silva said KOKO\u2019s achievement reflects progress across Sri Lanka\u2019s digital payments ecosystem, strengthening adoption and customer experience.\n\nToday, KOKO serves roughly 2 million users across approximately 6,500 merchants, positioning itself not only as the BNPL category leader but also as a major force in the country\u2019s broader digital payment landscape.\n\nThe awards ceremony was attended by key leaders including Deputy Minister of Digital Economy Eng. Eranga Weeraratne, Central Bank Governor Dr. P. Nandalal Weerasinghe, and Dr. Hans Wijayasuriya, Chief Advisor to the President on Digital Economy.\n\nApparel sector faces a global slowdown, JAAF undertakes quiet introspection\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
