    "chunk_size_bytes": 1762,
    "chunk_text": "Gnanaponrajah was part of the fraud in signing those cheques for grocery purchases, or else he was fiduciarily in cahoots for signing cheques whose genuineness he had not verified. Either way he deserved sacking as a minimum punishment. But no action was taken. After all, he is a priest!\n\nEven God is dragged into the mud by this church and fraudulent archdeacon as a cruel person for striking down those who expose corrupt priests.\n\nWill the bishop say why the Church took no action against Gnanaponrajah?\n\nGnanaponrajah\u2019s special episcopal dispensation from punishment does not end there. Mr. Vinoth was a master at St. John\u2019s. He accused Gnanaponrajah of making homosexual advances towards him. When this went on with no ending in sight, I was on the Standing Committee. Vinoth had recorded Gnanaponrajah\u2019s questionable begging overtures to be his friend.\u00a0 Bishop Dilo took no action.\n\nI informed him that the law requires a police report and that I would make a report if the church does not. He promised me he would get a senior District Judge to inquire. Finally, a young woman lawyer inquired. We were not privy to the report.\u00a0 At that time, another St. James\u2019 Warden, of the Paraya-caste himself,\u00a0 filmed a young low-caste Hindu OL girl bathing at her well. My wife and I both verified the facts. But Fr. Gnanakarunyan, a Paraya Priest, denied it and asked \u2018where is the proof? The offending boys\u2019 family headed by a bank manager came home\u00a0 and threatened to become Hindus unless we dropped the matter. It was getting messy.\n\nIn that recording, of Gnanaponrajah\u2019s overtures, initially a staff member is also present and the discussion is on school matters. After about the first 2 minutes, the overtures asking Vinoth to be his friend."
