    "chunk_size_bytes": 1612,
    "chunk_text": "In that recording, of Gnanaponrajah\u2019s overtures, initially a staff member is also present and the discussion is on school matters. After about the first 2 minutes, the overtures asking Vinoth to be his friend.\n\nHe\u00a0 works with boy scouts in Mullaitivu. Some old boys were planning to complain to the ministry because in a famous US Supreme Court case, as reported in Time, the court allowed the scouts to maintain their ban on gay scout masters (vide Boy Scouts of America Versus Dale 2000). In June that year, the U.S. Supreme Court ruled that the Boy Scouts had a constitutional right to exclude openly gay people from leadership positions, overturning a New Jersey Supreme Court decision. As recently as 2020 Time  records testimony from boy scouts about how scout masters abused them. At St. John\u2019s friends have told me of particular masters who abused them during the annual Jamboree at Old Park. We all knew who they were but the school did nothing. A senior doctor at Save the Children cried as he testified how badly he was abused at Trinity College hostel while the church did nothing.\n\nIn the end, Vinoth lost his job. Gnanaponrajah had done well. Boy scouts are allowed to suffer even in late age. That is JCU-Anglican social justice!\n\nAt that point a decision was taken somewhere to ensure that I am not to be re-elected to the Standing Committee. In Anglican make-believe devolution, at each Area Deanery an election is held to determine who would represent that region. At the pre-council meeting it was decided unanimously that I would represent the Northern Deanery at the Standing Committee."
