    "chunk_size_bytes": 1962,
    "chunk_text": "At that point a decision was taken somewhere to ensure that I am not to be re-elected to the Standing Committee. In Anglican make-believe devolution, at each Area Deanery an election is held to determine who would represent that region. At the pre-council meeting it was decided unanimously that I would represent the Northern Deanery at the Standing Committee.\n\nParaphrasing St. Sir Thomas More, More told his assitant Richard Rich who perjured himself to become Attorney General for Wales, that he sold his soul for too little. More famously asks as I do Mrs Sahayaseelan: \u201cYou sold your soul to be a stooge against the Northern Deanery after giving your word \u2013\u00a0 merely to be the Bishop\u2019s stooge, breaking your solemn word to the Northern Deanery?\u201d\n\nThe bishop\u2019s trick appears to be to put unqualified people at the top like Bishop Kenneth Fernando\u2019s appointment of his nephew Eksith Fernando which was vetoed by the Supreme Court for lack of 10 years\u2019 teaching experience to be Warden of St. Thomas\u2019. Yet, Ponniah without ten years\u2019 teaching experience was found good enough to be St. John\u2019s principal. With a cowed down, low-caste membership, this works only in Jaffna. Father Steve Jebachelvan with a national university Peradeniya degree is consistently overlooked choosing people like Ponniah from the South married to a Sinhalese who willingly suck up. Jebachelvan has no ten years but is more qualified than Ponniah.\n\nSam Ponniah was sent abroad for what I do not know but he has returned without any tertiary degree recorded in the STC webpages to date, and is placed as chaplain at St. Thomas\u2019 with no mention of additional credentials after almost 2 years abroad. He says he earned a BA from the University of the South.\u00a0 If he has it, why does STC not flaunt it?\n\nIf he truly has a BA from University off the South,why does STC not proudly list it? Why go for another BA if the Pilimatalawa degree is good? Was he on holiday?"
