    "chunk_size_bytes": 1930,
    "chunk_text": "Sam Ponniah was sent abroad for what I do not know but he has returned without any tertiary degree recorded in the STC webpages to date, and is placed as chaplain at St. Thomas\u2019 with no mention of additional credentials after almost 2 years abroad. He says he earned a BA from the University of the South.\u00a0 If he has it, why does STC not flaunt it?\n\nIf he truly has a BA from University off the South,why does STC not proudly list it? Why go for another BA if the Pilimatalawa degree is good? Was he on holiday?\n\nIs Jealousy a factor? It appears that one qualifies in the Anglican Church by having no qualifications, and that is why the Bishop fired Fr. Daniel! The Bishop runs a GREEN CHURCH!\n\nIs there an ongoing plot among the Sinhalese and southern Tamils to ruin Jaffna Tamil roots in education? I increasingly think so.\n\nR. Vinoth \u2013 One Sacked for Thieving from the YMCA Now Governor of the Church\n\nChurch corruption shows through in a matter involving another Vinoth, R Vinoth,\u00a0 an Anglican from St. James\u2019 from depressed caste origins. A handsome Singer Company salesman who was President of the YMCA, he had arranged for an employee to stand guard while he spent time inside his office with two women. It was seen by Andrew Sujeevan who reported it against the advice of senior Anglicans. Loving justice he had to follow his conscience. At Pilimatalawa Theological College, he would tell on his Dean who distributed exam papers through him. In the end, Andrew was sacked while the Dean after a brief suspension is ensconced in a comfortable job near his home.\n\nThe church punishes only those lower down, not the Bishop\u2019s loved ones.\n\nVinoth was untouched for this offence but was sacked after duplicate receipts were found on his YMCA computer of purchasing a television set and other electrical items from SINGER Sri Lanka according to a YMCA high up who asked me to come as the next President but I could not."
