    "chunk_text": "Vinoth was untouched for this offence but was sacked after duplicate receipts were found on his YMCA computer of purchasing a television set and other electrical items from SINGER Sri Lanka according to a YMCA high up who asked me to come as the next President but I could not.\n\nVinoth being clever, soon rebuilt himself. He rose to a position in Gandhi Nilayam, the cultural centre of the Parayas in Ariyalai,\u00a0 and to be St. James\u2019 representative to the diocesan council. Under reserved seats for area deaneries, he became a member of the standing committee representing the Northern Deanery \u2013 effectively a Governor of the Church.\n\nThis illiterate Northern Representative questioned at the last AGM of St. James as to why we are receiving small amount of interest on trust funds. We could write to the diocese, requesting not to send small amounts, he averred.\n\nMr. S. Narendranathan a former teacher, hostel master and a VERY good friend of former Pricipal Gnanaponrajah taught Mathematics and Christianity for the middle school boys (usually homosexual prey). When the term exams were over he would request his boys to come home to see the marks. He was living in a rented room in front of Chundikuli Girls\u2019 College during 1990 to1995. Many boys who went to see the marks had homosexual advances made by him. Those who cooperated got good marks."
