    "chunk_text": "Mr. S. Narendranathan a former teacher, hostel master and a VERY good friend of former Pricipal Gnanaponrajah taught Mathematics and Christianity for the middle school boys (usually homosexual prey). When the term exams were over he would request his boys to come home to see the marks. He was living in a rented room in front of Chundikuli Girls\u2019 College during 1990 to1995. Many boys who went to see the marks had homosexual advances made by him. Those who cooperated got good marks.\n\nDid the school management ask no questions? Strange indeed! St. John\u2019s had become a homosexual paradise! What a reward!\n\nDoes the Bishop not know? Surely Archdeacon Selvan does. Or is he selectively exercising forgiveness for a sacked YMCA President who would probably ensure that he would be a yes-man to anything the Bishop wants? As northern deanery rep, he will not represent the North but the southern deaneries and the crookedness from the South in self-preservation.\n\nThe church has to free itself from southern caste-based hegemony, not just serve high-ups and southern power brokers. This is why I ceased to be Anglican.\n\nTwo Sundays ago, Rev. Nesakumar who abuses his expired venerable title still calling himself Venerable, announced from the pulpit that my name has been removed from the Membership roll. What does it mean when anyone can receive? Surely I am not excommunicated as according to chapter 40 of our Constitution, Canons and Rules (2007), \u201cCanon 3 \u2013 The Bishop of the Diocese alone has the power to pronounce the sentence of excommunication on a guilty person and shall only pronounce sentence after the facts of a case have been duly established by inquiry made by or under the Bishop\u2019s direction in accordance with the customs of the Church [\u2026] provided that before such sentence of excommunication is pronounced, the accused person must have received notice of all charges and have had an opportunity of being heard in defence.\u201d"
