    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s economic outlook brightens with Graphene\n\nAn exclusive business conclave for Investment Promotion on Graphene Technology held at Kingsbury Colombo last week aimed at promoting investment in graphene technology, attracting a robust presence of both local and international investors.\n\nThis high-level platform was orchestrated by Ragedara Graphite Mines Chairman Eng. Keerthi Wickramaratne , a pioneer in the mining, research, and production of vein graphite and graphene in Malsiripura, Sri Lanka.\n\nThe conclave served as a critical forum for discussing the future potential of graphene and its transformative impact across global industries. Key topics included the strategic importance of graphite and graphene as materials that could drive technological advancement and bolster national economic growth.\n\nEconomic Development Deputy Minister Nishantha Jayaweera noted encouraging news about Sri Lanka\u2019s economic outlook, acknowledging the private sector\u2019s role in creating value-added products for niche export markets, a sentiment echoed during the Graphene product launch.\n\n\u201cSri Lanka has achieved an improved stable economy status as we look towards the year 2025, surpassing our financial expectations this year, marking a significant victory,\u201d he stated. \u201cOur primary aim moving forward is to accelerate development and broaden our economy, consolidating Foreign Direct Investments (FDI) while attracting local investments. This reflects what the people expect from us,\u201d he emphasised.\n\nDeputy Minister Jayaweera also announced the introduction of three new acts designed to enhance investment opportunities in Sri Lanka: an Investment Protection Act, an Investment Promotion Act, and a Strategic Development Act. Additionally, he revealed a five-year Investment Diversification Plan aimed at achieving the government\u2019s specific goals, which includes potential tax relief for investment ventures in the Port City."
  },
