    "md5": "c6681b95c8b39746ea2b804bc3f84ef3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1221,
    "chunk_text": "Seychelles \u2026 here we come\n\nThe group Mirage left for the Seychelles last week for a three-week stint at the Lo Brizan pub/restaurant, Niva Labriz Resort.\n\nThis is their fifth trip to the Seychelles and, according to reports coming our way, the band is extremely popular at this particular venue.\n\n\u201cWe do six nights a week and we have a very enthusiastic crowd turning up every night which makes our work so enjoyable,\u201d says leader Donald Pieries, who has molded Mirage into a top-notch outfit.\n\nThey have two more foreign assignments cropping up, before the year is out, and they are also to the same venue in the Seychelles \u2013 Lo Brizan pub/restaurant, Niva Labriz Resort \u2013 in August and December.\n\nThere is also talk that a trip to Australia may work out for Mirage, before the year ends!\n\nObviously, their music will be missed by local music lovers but the scene here is a bit dicey with work, for performers, a bit hard to come by.\n\nNew arithmetic of conflict: How the drone revolution is inverting economics of war\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
