    "chunk_text": "Yesterday the rupee was quoted at Rs 314.75/315.25 to the US dollar in the spot market, depreciating further from Rs 314.70/315.00 the previous day, dealers said, while bond yields opened slightly higher with the market a bit quiet.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2029 was quoted at 9.95/10.00 percent, up from 9.80/90 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.03.2031 was quoted at 10.05/15 percent, up from 10.00/10 percent.\n\nThe rupee was quoted at 309.20/25 to the US dollar in the spot market on February 28, the day before the US and Israel bombed Iran.\n\nThe telegraphic transfer rates for the American dollar were 311.2500 buying, 318.2500 selling; the British pound was 411.4501 buying, and 422.7535 selling, and the euro was 355.8446 buying, 367.2640 selling.\n\nMiddle East Conflict: The impact on migration and remittances in Sri Lanka\n\nOil tops $116 a barrel as Iran accuses US of preparing invasion\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
