    "md5": "a873ac77e4123b3d973b437fe9410849",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1971,
    "chunk_text": "Export values declared in returns are fully aligned with Customs data.\n\nEven minor errors or mismatches can trigger system-generated notices, pausing the statutory refund timeline until the necessary corrections are made.\n\nAccurate reconciliation of VAT returns with Customs data is critical for both imports and exports. Accurate alignment ensures valid input VAT claims, timely refunds, and mitigates audit risk.\n\nInput VAT on imported goods must be reconciled with Customs Declarations (CUSDEC), including invoice value, VAT paid, customs duties, importer TIN, and import date.\n\nMinor variances may be tolerated if documented and justifiable, but material discrepancies can trigger audits or disallowances.\n\nIn practice, there are instances where the IRD may require that claims be reflected in the VAT return for the import period, even though the statutory 24-month window provides flexibility. Therefore, taxpayers should take proactive steps to include the claim in the VAT return without undue delay.\n\nMinor variances may be tolerated but can still impact risk ratings.\n\nDifferences exceeding acceptable thresholds (typically above 10%) require formal reconciliation and explanation.\n\nRepeated mismatches may result in a high-risk classification and trigger pre-refund verification.\n\nMaintaining accurate import and export records and performing timely reconciliations is essential to ensure smooth and efficient VAT refund processing, mitigate risk, and align with the IRD\u2019s practical compliance expectations.\n\nUnder the new system, VAT refunds are increasingly documentation-driven. Taxpayers must be able to produce supporting documents on short notice, including:\n\nPoor document management often leads to repeated requests from the IRD and extended verification, even when claims are otherwise valid.\n\nMaintain refund-specific documentation folders (physical or digital) for each taxable period to ensure quick access and avoid last-minute retrieval issues."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-03-31-dailyftlk-9604cb19",
    "num": "dailyftlk-9604cb19",
    "date_str": "2026-03-31",
    "description": "Navigating Sri Lanka\u2019s new VAT refund framework: Key compliance insights",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/columns/Navigating-Sri-Lanka-s-new-VAT-refund-framework-Key-compliance-insights/4-790271",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
