    "md5": "beb51a9a494d82013acf6c0c57af7078",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1941,
    "chunk_text": "Outdated taxpayer profiles are a common and avoidable cause of refund delays under the new system. Taxpayers should ensure that the following details are accurately maintained in Revenue Administration Management Information System (RAMIS):\n\nMissed notices or communications due to outdated information can result in suspended refunds, even when claims are otherwise valid.\n\nRequests for documents or clarifications typically allow only a limited response period.\n\nFailure to respond may result in refund rejection, rather than a simple delay.\n\nAssign clear responsibility for monitoring IRD communications daily to ensure timely responses and avoid unnecessary delays or disallowances.\n\nVAT refund claims are reviewed in the context of any outstanding tax balances. Key considerations include:\n\nEngaging proactively with the Tax Default Recovery Unit of the IRD can help clarify set-off positions and prevent unexpected deductions, ensuring smoother refund processing.\n\nUnder the risk-based VAT refund system, taxpayers classified as high risk should anticipate additional verification measures, which may include:\n\nRefund delays often result not from the verification itself, but from incomplete or delayed responses during the process. Timely and thorough engagement is therefore essential for efficient refund processing.\n\nOverstated or inadequately documented refund claims significantly increase the likelihood of enhanced scrutiny under the risk-based system. Taxpayers should ensure they avoid:\n\nA well-supported, conservative claim is far more likely to be processed efficiently than an aggressive or poorly substantiated one, reducing the risk of delays, verification, or rejection.\n\nEven for compliant taxpayers, practical issues may arise during the VAT refund process due to system validations, data mismatches, or verification requirements. Knowing where to seek assistance can help resolve issues promptly and minimise delays."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
