    "language": "en",
    "md5": "3024385a42bbe0dd740def7e79dc07ad",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1304,
    "chunk_text": "Even for compliant taxpayers, practical issues may arise during the VAT refund process due to system validations, data mismatches, or verification requirements. Knowing where to seek assistance can help resolve issues promptly and minimise delays.\n\nIRD Call Centre \u2013 1944: for clarification on notices, document requests, and refund status.\n\nConsultation and Promotion Units at IRD Head Office or Regional Offices: for in-person guidance.\n\nExport Refund Processing Unit: for exporter-specific refund matters and prolonged verification cases.\n\nMaintaining proper records of all communications and submissions is essential when seeking assistance to ensure accountability and efficient resolution.\n\nUnder Sri Lanka\u2019s new risk-based VAT refund system, securing timely refunds depends less on statutory entitlement alone and more on effective practical compliance management. Key factors influencing refund processing now include:\n\nTaxpayers who proactively address these practical considerations are far more likely to enjoy faster refunds, fewer audits, and smoother interactions with the IRD. Conversely, a reactive approach increases the risk of prolonged delays, verification, or even rejection under the new system.\n\n(The author is Senior Manager \u2013 Tax and Business Advisory, Deloitte Sri Lanka.)"
  },
