    "md5": "4aa9946c7e3e74e1d4af07e02ef9d63c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1691,
    "chunk_text": "Cap Snap Lanka receives six international certifications including ISO-FSSC\n\nDirector and Group Consultant Hugh Indrajith, Director and Group Chief Executive Officer Farih Fazal, Chairman Anura Kumarasinghe, Managing Director M.H.M. Fazal, and Bureau Veritas Sri Lanka Country General Manager Shan Nanayakkara and his team\n\nCap Snap Lanka Ltd., a member of the CSL Group, has received six internationally recognised certifications, including the Food Safety System Certification (FSSC 22000), at a ceremony held recently in Colombo. The achievement is particularly noteworthy as all six certifications were secured within just six months, reflecting the company\u2019s strong commitment to quality, safety, and operational excellence. The certifications were awarded by Bureau Veritas Sri Lanka Country General Manager Shan Nanayakkara and his team in the presence of the Cap Snap Lanka leadership. The event also included a presentation on the company\u2019s history and operations, followed by a corporate video showcasing its 20-year journey in the plastics and rigid packaging industry. Chief Operating Officer Rizwan Jalill was also present at the ceremony. The certifications were formally presented to Chairman Anura Kumarasinghe, Managing Director M.H.M. Fazal, Director and Group Chief Executive Officer Farih Fazal, and Director and Group Consultant Hugh Indrajith. The certifications received by the company were ISO 9001:2015 for Quality Management, ISO 14001:2015 for Environmental Management, Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP), Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points (HACCP), ISO 22000:2018 for Food Safety Management, and FSSC 22000 Version 6 under GFSI Food Safety standards."
  },
