    "chunk_size_bytes": 1790,
    "chunk_text": "OPPO launches Reno 15 Series\n\nOPPO Sri Lanka recently launched its latest smartphone lineup, the Reno 15 Series, at the Abans showroom in Havelock City Mall\u00a0 marking the official entry of the device range into the local market while announcing plans to further strengthen its investment in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe launch event brought together leading influencers, technology key opinion leaders (KOLs), media representatives and industry stakeholders, reflecting OPPO\u2019s growing presence and strategic focus on the Sri Lankan market. The company stated that the initiative is aimed at delivering enhanced consumer experiences, improved product accessibility and long-term brand value.\n\nCompany representatives also expressed appreciation for the continued trust and recognition shown by Sri Lankan consumers, noting that OPPO remains committed to continuous improvement and innovation to meet evolving customer needs.\n\nThe Reno 15 Series is positioned to cater to modern digital lifestyles, particularly targeting creators, gamers and digital-first users. The event featured strong influencer participation, with real-time content creation and social media engagement amplifying the launch across multiple platforms.\n\nAttendees were given hands-on access to the devices through interactive experience zones, enabling them to explore key features including camera capabilities, gaming performance and overall design. The approach reflects OPPO\u2019s emphasis on consumer-centric engagement and experiential marketing.\n\nIn terms of design, the Reno 15 Series introduces a premium aesthetic inspired by the \u201cDancing Aurora\u201d concept. The device features a light-reflective finish with dynamic colour transitions, offering a sleek and modern appearance while maintaining a comfortable in-hand feel."
  },
