    "description": "LankaPay launched cross border QR payments acceptance via Weixin Pay at LANKAQR merchants",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/LankaPay-launched-cross-border-QR-payments-acceptance-via-Weixin-Pay-at-LANKAQR-merchants/34-790351",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1775006751.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-04-01-dailyftlk-646c3a49-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8ccf088155daff963fff2b2d019f0e8d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1346,
    "chunk_text": "LankaPay launched cross border QR payments acceptance via Weixin Pay at LANKAQR merchants\n\nFrom left: LankaPay Senior Manager \u2013 Global Operations Harsha de Silva, Deputy CEO Dinuka Perera, CEO Channa de Silva, Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau Chairman Buddhika Hewawasam,\u00a0 Weixin Pay Country Manager David Chong,\u00a0 Senior Manager Laura Wang and Senior Manager Calvin Thye\n\nLankaPay, Sri Lanka\u2019s National Payment Network, recently announced its partnership with Weixin Pay (popularly known as WeChat Pay)\u00a0 to enable cross border QR payment acceptance at LANKAQR merchants at a launch held at NH Collection, Colombo.\n\nThrough this collaboration, Weixin Pay customers travelling to Sri Lanka will be able to seamlessly scan and pay at over 400,000 LANKAQR merchants island wide, significantly enhancing Sri Lanka\u2019s cross-border digital payment capabilities. The initiative is expected to improve payment convenience for inbound tourists and business travelers while supporting the growth of the country\u2019s tourism sector.\n\nWeixin Pay, one of the world\u2019s leading mobile payment platforms, is widely used by the Chinese mainland travelers. With this integration, tourists using Weixin Pay will be able to pay conveniently during their visit in Sri Lanka, enabling the same the payment experience as they are used to in their home country."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-04-01-dailyftlk-646c3a49",
    "num": "dailyftlk-646c3a49",
    "date_str": "2026-04-01",
    "description": "LankaPay launched cross border QR payments acceptance via Weixin Pay at LANKAQR merchants",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.ft.lk/business/LankaPay-launched-cross-border-QR-payments-acceptance-via-Weixin-Pay-at-LANKAQR-merchants/34-790351",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailyftlk",
    "time_ut": 1775006751.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-04-01-dailyftlk-646c3a49-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "e3072b2b27ecb4c7e0d69aa0a1c86d3f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1872,
    "chunk_text": "Weixin Pay, one of the world\u2019s leading mobile payment platforms, is widely used by the Chinese mainland travelers. With this integration, tourists using Weixin Pay will be able to pay conveniently during their visit in Sri Lanka, enabling the same the payment experience as they are used to in their home country.\n\nLankaPay Chief Executive Officer Channa de Silva said: \u201cWe are extremely pleased to enable Weixin Pay acceptance in Sri Lanka. This collaboration reflects our continued commitment to providing secure, seamless, and internationally interoperable payment solutions. By connecting global travelers with Sri Lanka\u2019s LANKAQR network, we aim to enhance payment convenience while supporting local merchants and contributing to the broader growth of the economy.\u201d\n\nWeixin Pay\u2019s Managing Director for Southeast Asia and North America Ben Yang said: \u201cWe are delighted to collaborate with LankaPay to introduce Weixin Pay in Sri Lanka. As China\u2019s outbound travel continues to expand, the availability of familiar and convenient payment options is increasingly important. This partnership will enable travellers to transact seamlessly while offering local businesses new opportunities to engage with global customers.\u201d\n\nLANKAQR, introduced under the guidance of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, ensures that all QR-based transactions in the country are standardised and interoperable complying with international EMVCo standards. Operated by LankaPay, the network connects banks, financial institutions, merchants, and consumers onto a single platform, facilitating secure and efficient digital payments nationwide.\n\nWith the launch of Weixin Pay acceptance, LankaPay further strengthens its position as a key enabler of Sri Lanka\u2019s digital payment infrastructure and continues to drive innovation in support of the country\u2019s evolving digital economy."
  },
